msgid "Policy track · MTechnical track · TPolicyDay 1M1M2M3Day 2M4M5M6M7TechnicalDay 1T1T2T3T4T5Day 2T6T7 DPI-H for Health workshop · Convergence Bangkok 2026Two tracks, seven modules each, one journeyEach policy module asks one question of the journey and fills one sheet of the Country Canvas. Each technical module is paired with the policy module of the same number. Policy track Day 1 · 30 November M1Sheet 1From journey to capabilitiesWhat had to exist for this moment to work — and where does our version of the journey break?J1J3a M2Sheet 2The reference architecture and where you standWhich system do we use today for each block — and is it there, partly there, or absent?J2b M3Sheet 3Standards, specifications and the core data setWhich standards do we adopt rather than author — and who owns the national core data set?J2aJ3b  Day 2 · 1 December M4Sheet 4Trust, credentials and walletsWho signs, who verifies, and who would hold the national trust anchor? Name it; do not decide it.J1J2aJ3aJ4.0a M5Sheet 4Governance, decision rights and the legal basisWho holds each decision — and what legal basis lets the record cross a border and be shared for a child?J1J2bJ4.0aJ4.0bJ4.1 M6Sheet 5Doing it togetherWould your neighbour need this too? If yes, why would you each build it?J3bJ4.0bJ4.1 M7Sheet 6First move and the investment requiredWhat is realistic in twelve months with the people and money we have — and who owns it?J4.1  Technical track DraftTwo days, one cross-border immunization story. Day 1 covers the building blocks and gets everyone running on Heropa. Day 2 is teams building one part of the journey, then seeing it all work together. Draft for the team to confirm. Names and times are proposals. Day 1 · 30 November · Concepts and the OHS stack. By the end of the day you have captured data, synced it, run a workflow and started a dashboard, all on Heropa. T111:00–11:40Building with FHIR and the Open Health StackWhich FHIR resources, terminologies and tools carry this journey, and where does each lab use them?J1J3bJ4.0b T211:40–12:30Offline data captureHow does a form on a health worker's phone become a patient record, with no signal?J2aJ2b T313:30–13:50Trust between countries: SMART Trust and the GDHCNHow can a clinic in one country trust a vaccination record from another, and when is a card better than a link?J1J3aJ4.1 T413:50–15:00Workflows, sync and who sees whatWhat should happen next for this child, how does the record reach the server, and who is allowed to see it?J2bJ3bJ4.0bJ4.1 T515:30–16:30From records to chartsHow does a FHIR record become a row, a chart and a coverage number, and who accessed what?J2bJ3bJ4.1  Day 2 · 1 December · Teams build one app in the journey, show it, and then everything runs together. T611:00–11:30Verifying a card, sharing a linkHow does an app go from a scanned QR to a verified result, and from a shared link to the records behind it?J3aJ4.0bJ4.1 T711:30–16:15Team build, showcase and the journey togetherCan each team change one app in the journey and then run the whole journey live, from a birth abroad to a clinic back home to the family travelling again?J2bJ3aJ4.0aJ4.1  Still to confirmCarl to confirm the Day 1 trust talk, 13:30 to 13:50.Joint sessions on both days to be agreed with the policy track, including who leads the two 16:30 slots.Heropa classroom test late next week. Day 2 apps need an emulator or the Wasm web build, since nobody installs Android Studio.Lab 3: confirm Observable Framework, the shared test data, and Matt's help once the apps are seeded.Which facilitator takes which Day 2 team.A short recording of the full journey as a fallback for the finale. Module × journey mapCountry CanvasGlossaryJourneys viewer"
